Incident INC-260713 is resolved as of 14:31 UTC.

Between 13:52 and 14:24 UTC, Checkout SVC-17 returned elevated 502 responses
when the regional payment-routing pool retried an upstream dependency. The
service error budget is now 2.4% remaining for the current window. Customer
orders were not duplicated; unsuccessful checkout attempts can be retried
normally.

The on-call SRE drained the unhealthy routing targets and restored the prior
retry ceiling. The error rate has remained below the paging threshold for seven
minutes, checkout latency is within the operating range, and synthetic purchase
checks are passing in both active regions.

Next steps:
- The incident commander will keep the bridge open through the 15:00 UTC check.
- Checkout Operations will attach the request-trace sample to the incident
  record before end of shift.
- The SRE rotation will publish the five-whys and corrective actions by
  16 Jul, with the change record linked to INC-260713.

Please use the incident record for follow-up rather than starting a new paging
thread.
